/target
/references
__pycache__/

# machine-local agent tool state
.codegraph/
.serena/
.opencode/

# stray runtime pidfiles
*.pid

# personal agent working files — never leave this machine
/AGENTS.md
/MEMORY.md
/MEMORY-archive-*.md

# nuclear-audit working ledgers
/.audit/

# bench campaign outputs (raw cells.jsonl, charts, media outputs, dumps,
# reports) stay local by default. A small exception set is force-added past
# these rules and listed by `git ls-files bench-artifacts`: INDEX.md, the
# charts BENCHMARK.md embeds, and the receipts that a registry, doc, README
# link or code comment cites. `python3 scripts/bench_archive.py` prints that
# set; run it after a campaign, because `--apply` force-adds newly cited
# reports, untracks reports nothing cites and writes the archive tarball for
# the bench-archive GitHub release (commit the index afterwards). Without
# it scripts/engine_coverage.py --check fails with "receipt artifact
# missing" in a fresh clone.
# Regenerate charts from cells with scripts/bench_charts.py.
# staging/ symlinks point at user-local models; cells-stderr/ is
# debugging-only; corpus.txt captures working-tree prose incl. machine
# paths.
bench-artifacts/**
!bench-artifacts/**/
!bench-artifacts/INDEX.md

# playwright-cli session scratch: console/page snapshots from local
# browser validation runs — debugging-only, regenerable on demand.
.playwright-cli/
*.egg-info/

# TypeScript SDK dev install (never shipped)
sdk/ts/node_modules/
